                                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                                    "patching_rect": [ 348.0, 63.0, 173.0, 60.0 ],
                                                    "text": "you can change preset from outside by sending in the first inlet the preset number (int or float) with a prepend \"preset\" "
                                                }
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "box": {
                                                    "id": "obj-3",
                                                    "linecount": 35,
                                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                                    "patching_rect": [ 6.0, 67.0, 316.0, 489.0 ],
                                                    "text": "snippet built around petra's [cm.indexcloud~]\n\ndon't know what granular synthesys is?\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Granular_synthesis\n\ndefine a range of your sample you want to granularize and granular~ will randomly play grains withing that time range\n\nyou can drop and audio file in the field\n\nstart: the starting point (in milliseconds) of the range (orange selection) to granularize \n\nstartRnd: the additive randomization of the grain start in milliseconds (smaller orange selection)\n\npitch: pitch multiplier of grains, 2= octave up, 0.5= actave down\n\nlength: how long are the single grains (in milliseconds)\n\nlenghtRnd: the additive randomization of the grain length in milliseconds (smaller orange selection)\n\ndensity: how often (in Hz) is a grain played\n\namplitude: how loud? 0 = mute\n\nreverse: reverse the playback of grains\n\nbuffer name: this is the automatically assigned name of the internal buffer~ in case you want to copy it and address it from outside\n\n"
                                                }
                                            },
